data seed_growth_admission_note: String = "ITEM-GRAIN admission authority for hand-authored Rust growth (Lane swift-lynx-164). TARGET: compare every newly authored or modified hand Rust item in a change against SeedGrowthJustification.hand_authored_declarations and refuse on the difference (gunbc.seed_growth.seed_growth_note completeness join). PATH-GRAIN census answers which files lack disposition; THIS MODULE answers which ITEMS within files lack justification. NOT IN SCOPE: deleting existing Rust. NOT IN SCOPE: netting deletions against additions -- and that is now EXECUTED rather than merely stated: no arm of seed_growth_admit_change reads deleted_hand_items, and seed_growth_deletions_offset_nothing runs one unjustified addition through two observations whose deleted populations differ and requires one verdict. It is a WITNESSED property and not a structural one -- the observation record still carries the deleted population, so a future arm could read it -- and the honest rung is the witness, not the shape. THE G0 HOST EXISTS AGAIN. scripts/rust_item_census.py was deleted by gunbc#9132 and the capability went to zero with it, undeclared, because the census's consumers were lanes rather than modules and no dependent could refuse. gunbc.rust_item_host_observation replaces it: two populations from two functions, item extraction through gunbc.rust_item_scan whose item-keyword population is READ FROM the extdeps.languages.rust grammar authority rather than re-coined as the deleted script's regex ITEM_PATTERNS were. ENROLLED: seed_growth_roster_well_formed_gate_holds (roster well-formedness) and seed_growth_admit_change (the completeness join against a real changed-item population). WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: no required CI phase invokes the join yet, so the rung is the ROUTE existing and its wall executing under witnesses -- not a gate armed on every push. Arming it is a claim_executor phase, which is itself hand-Rust growth this very join would have to admit, and it lands separately."

// THE MODIFIED POPULATION IS REPORTED AND NOT YET REFUSED, AND SAYING WHICH IS THE POINT.
//
// A modification is the arm that decides whether this construction does anything: a worker can add
// an entire capability to an existing two-thousand-line function without creating one new item, so
// an admission that only refused ADDITIONS would leave the freeze open through the largest
// functions in the seed. The rule that governs it is that a modification may not ORIGINATE semantic
// capability in Rust, which is what ExistingSeedItemModified's capability_origin states.
//
// What is NOT here is a roster of those dispositions, and its absence is deliberate rather than
// forgotten: the terminal roster closes with the final claim_executor cut, and hand-transcribing it
// today would mean authoring roughly fifteen hundred moving declarations that can omit items while
// staying internally well-formed -- rung inflation wearing a roster. So this field makes the
// population VISIBLE and COUNTABLE, which is what a later roster needs to be derivable at all, and
// the refusal lands with that roster. Reporting it is weaker than refusing it and is labelled so.
type SeedGrowthAdmissionVerdict
  = SeedGrowthAdmissionComplete {
      justified_items: List<String>,
      modified_items_requiring_disposition: List<String>,
      stale_justifications: List<String>,
      duplicate_justifications: List<String>,
      uncitable_items: List<String>
    }
  | SeedGrowthAdmissionRefused {
      unjustified_additions: List<String>,
      detail: String
    }

// A MODIFICATION CARRIES ITS CAPABILITY ORIGIN, AND THAT FIELD IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THE ARM.
//
// ExistingSeedItemModified without it reads as "the item already existed, therefore anything may be
// added to it" -- and a worker can add an ENTIRE CAPABILITY to an existing two-thousand-line
// function without creating one new Rust item. Under that reading the forward freeze is reopened
// through the largest functions in the seed and the whole construction is decorative, refusing only
// the additions nobody needed to hide. So the arm states where the capability came from:
// NoNewCapability (the edit originates none) or ModeledCapability carrying where the model came
// from. There is deliberately no value naming a capability originated in Rust, because that is the
// state the freeze forbids; it is unrepresentable rather than checked, which is the construction
// direction DESIGN section 5 asks for.
//
// THE VOCABULARY MOVED TO gunbc.capability_origin AND GREW A PAYLOAD, AND THE PAYLOAD IS THE
// CORRECTION. CapabilityAlreadyModeled stood here and was payload-free, so it could be satisfied by
// inspecting the final candidate -- which cannot distinguish a model that existed before its
// realization from a model added beside the realization that inspired it, and that distinction is
// the entire question the arm exists to ask. It now names its authority and, when the authority is
// itself new in this change, the independent ground that makes it prior.
//
// THE SAME RELATION GOVERNS ADDITIONS, which is the half an admission wall loses first: a newly
// added item can carry a perfectly good justification row and still have been retro-modeled in the
// same change, so seed_growth_admit_change asks both questions of every addition rather than
// treating roster membership as sufficient.

type SeedGrowthChangeDisposition
  = SeedBridgeAuthorized
  | ExistingSeedItemModified {
      item: DeclarationRef,
      dag_authority: DeclarationRef,
      capability_origin: CapabilityOrigin,
      current_boundary: String
    }
  | GeneratedInstead
  | HandRustDeleted
  | RetainedKernel
  | GrowthRefused

data seed_growth_forward_freeze_policy_note: String = "THE STOP-LINE HAS A MECHANISM AGAIN, AND THIS ROW STATES ITS RUNG RATHER THAN ITS AMBITION. Every PR that adds hand-written src/v1 Rust MUST enumerate: exact item identity, .dag authority, why Rust is still needed, owning lane, deletion trigger, current boundary. Unenumerated hand growth is a stop-line -- no netting deletions against additions, which seed_growth_deletions_offset_nothing now executes rather than merely instructing: no arm of seed_growth_admit_change reads the deleted population, and the witness runs one addition through two observations whose deletions differ and requires one verdict. Generated Rust is exempt only with generation-authority proof (gunbc.stage0_rust_source_lifecycle_scaffold derived_generated_stage0_repo_paths or gunbc.generated_artifact), and that classification is now DERIVED by gunbc.rust_item_host_observation rather than asserted by the author. THIS ROW SAID (enforceable now) UNTIL 2026-08-24 AND THAT WAS RUNG INFLATION; it then said no mechanism could refuse hand growth, which was true until this change. MEASURED, and it is why the mechanism was worth building rather than the policy worth restating: of the four PRs that added hand src/v1 Rust in the 48 hours to 2026-08-24, ZERO were caught by an unassisted reviewer -- all four were caught by a follow-up investigation after they had already reached approval. THE TWO CONDITIONS THIS ROW SET ON ENROLMENT ARE BOTH MET, and they are recorded as met rather than deleted, because a condition that vanishes when it is satisfied leaves the next author unable to tell whether it was answered or forgotten. FIRST, THE JOIN IS SPLIT: seed_growth_unjustified_additions reads the CHANGE population and seed_growth_stale_justifications reads the LIVE population, so a justification for an untouched item is no longer rendered stale by a change population, and a live population no longer hides what this change added. SECOND, THE EXTRACTOR REFUSES RATHER THAN REPORTING AN EMPTY DELTA: every arm of RustItemChangeObservation that could not attribute a changed hand-Rust region is a typed, located refusal, and seed_growth_admit_change maps each of them to SeedGrowthAdmissionRefused rather than to a complete verdict with an empty list. RUNG: mechanically preventable AS TO THE ROUTE, and no higher -- the wall executes under witnesses and is callable, and NO REQUIRED CI PHASE INVOKES IT YET. A mechanism no lane runs guards nothing, and calling this armed would be the inflation DESIGN section 4b(1) names as worse than sitting low. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a required-run phase that computes the change observation and stops the line on SeedGrowthAdmissionRefused. ALSO DERIVABLE, NOT AUTHORED: hand-item delta and hand-LOC delta are functions of the diff, so requiring an author to type them creates a second representation of a fact the diff already owns (DESIGN 2) -- and the cost was measured, a seed-growth receipt on gunbc#9095 claiming +195/+65 against a measured +203/-0, +60/-5, +102/-0. They are dropped from the enumeration above as of this change, because the observation now derives them and an authored copy would be exactly that second representation."

// CLOSED ROSTER of every SeedGrowthJustification row in the corpus. G1 joins new/modified hand
// items against this list. Rows are authored beside the obligation they declare. THE LIVE
// POPULATION IS seed_growth_justification_roster(), AND IT IS THE ONLY AUTHORITY -- this row no
// longer enumerates it. Each new justification adds one entry to that function AND one data row in
// its owning module; it adds nothing here.
//
// WHY THE ENUMERATION WAS DELETED (2026-08-25). This sentence used to name every row, which made
// the prose and the function two WRITABLE AUTHORITIES over one population, and they diverged in
// both directions. The correctness defect: gunbc#9089 added its import and its function entry
// without naming its row here, so the function carried four while the prose said three, and nothing
// could detect it -- a row missing from the prose but present in the function conflicts with
// nothing, so no merge ever asks anyone to reconcile them. The operational symptom: across six
// consecutive roster unions on 2026-08-24/25, seed_growth_justification_roster() AUTO-MERGED every
// single time and this sentence was the ONLY conflict in the file. Six for six. Two representations
// of one fact, one of which a merge tool can reconcile and one of which it cannot -- so only the
// unreconcilable one generated work, and it was the one with no authority. DESIGN section 2,
// measured rather than argued.
//
// WHAT IS NOT REPLACED, because deleting a prose row takes everything in it unless the contents are
// enumerated first. No renderer is built: nothing consumes a rendered list of row names, and
// building one to preserve prose that should not exist would re-create the second representation in
// executable form. No parallel List<DeclarationRef> is added either, for the same reason one
// function and one sentence failed -- two executable rosters drift exactly as prose and function
// did. IF a consumer ever needs each row's own declaration identity (the mechanical seed-growth
// join will, since it needs exact identities for diagnostics), the fix is to pair identity and
// value in ONE entry at construction -- a SeedGrowthJustificationEntry carrying { row:
// DeclarationRef, justification: SeedGrowthJustification } -- never a second list beside the first.
// Until such a consumer exists, deleting the duplication is the whole change.
//
// BOTH SIDES OF A ROSTER MERGE ARE STILL KEPT: this is a closed roster, so taking either side of a
// conflict whole silently deletes the other branch's authority obligation rather than conflicting.
// That rule now applies to the function list alone, which is where it was always load-bearing and
// where git has in practice resolved it correctly every time.

// UNCITABLE ITEMS (prose-only until std.decl_ref gains ImplMethod). stage0_rust_observation_seed_growth_justification documents one: impl std::fmt::Display for Stage0CargoBinManifestParseRefusal in v1_compiler.cli_run — seven hand items, six citable DeclarationRef rows. G1 reports uncitable_items separately; they do NOT satisfy the forward-freeze enumeration via DeclarationRef alone.
// SCAFFOLD ROWS RETIRED, AND THE RETIREMENT IS RECORDED RATHER THAN SILENT.
//
// Two Scaffold dispositions stood here. seed_growth_admission_join_scaffold marked
// seed_growth_join_declarations as not-an-admission-gate "until rust_item_host_observation supplies
// diff DeclarationRef candidates"; that function is gone, replaced by the split pair below, and the
// candidates now exist. seed_growth_g0_census_host_scaffold marked scripts/rust_item_census.py, and
// stated its trigger as the two clauses it always was: (a) the script deleted -- satisfied by
// gunbc#9132 rather than by this lane, and (b) a producer enrolling -- outstanding until now. Both
// clauses are met, so the row retires by its own terms rather than by an author's judgement.
//
// THE HALF-FIRED TRIGGER IS THE LESSON AND IT IS KEPT. Clause (a) was satisfied by an unrelated cut
// that restored nothing, which is precisely the shape DESIGN section 4b(3) forbids when it requires
// a restoration trigger to name the CAPABILITY rather than an artifact that would contribute to
// one: for three days the disposition read half-discharged while the thing it existed to protect
// was entirely absent. gunbc.rust_item_identity rust_item_host_observation_producer_note carries
// that receipt at the site where the trigger was written.
data seed_growth_admission_g0_population_note: String = "G0 CENSUS HOST: gunbc.rust_item_host_observation. Population is measured at execution from revision-addressed .rs blobs; generated-versus-hand is DERIVED from gunbc.stage0_rust_source_lifecycle_scaffold derived_generated_stage0_repo_paths and gunbc.generated_artifact artifact_path, and a path no namespace row claims REFUSES rather than acquiring a plausible module path. This note pins no numeric literals (DESIGN section 3 stale-citation class) and names no transcribed measurement: the instrument is the function, and a figure is read by running it. G1 -- the comparison of the merge-base-to-HEAD change against SeedGrowthJustification rows -- is seed_growth_admit_change below."

fn seed_growth_justification_roster() -> List<SeedGrowthJustification> {
  [
    anonymous_record_resolution_seed_growth_justification,
    floor_non_verdict_seed_growth_justification,
    floor_route_gap_seed_growth_justification,
    floor_cost_debt_seed_growth_justification,
    cross_claim_pure_share_seed_growth_justification,
    cross_claim_demand_census_seed_growth_justification,
    frame_independent_symbol_seed_growth_justification,
    floor_cost_debt_standing_seed_growth_justification,
    floor_population_projection_seed_growth_justification,
    stage0_rust_observation_seed_growth_justification,
    observation_scoped_run_seed_growth_justification(),
    whole_corpus_compile_seed_growth_justification,
    reference_closure_binder_seed_growth_justification,
    bare_reference_scanner_seed_growth_justification,
    ambiguity_ban_seed_growth_justification,
    witness_runtime_cause_seed_growth_justification,
    parse_refusal_location_seed_growth_justification,
    claim_unwind_seed_growth_justification,
    claim_batch_function_preflight_seed_growth_justification,
    routed_entry_closure_membership_seed_growth_justification,
    shared_fill_attribution_seed_growth_justification,
    census_memo_seed_growth_justification,
    declaration_index_seed_growth_justification,
    emitted_closure_compile_seed_growth_justification,
    evaluation_budget_falsifier_seed_growth_justification,
    namespace_structural_observation_bridge_seed_growth_justification,
    parsed_import_statement_bridge_seed_growth_justification,
    namespace_wave_admission_seed_growth_justification,
    qualified_pipe_callee_seed_growth_justification,
    target_invocation_seed_growth_justification,
    bootstrap_operation_seed_growth_justification,
    cli_dispatch_host_boundary_seed_growth_justification,
    generated_artifact_boundary_seed_growth_justification,
    regen_convergence_seed_growth_justification,
    decl_facts_shared_memo_seed_growth_justification,
    cli_wire_host_seed_growth_justification,
    filesystem_create_new_seed_growth_justification,
    required_lane_judgment_seed_growth_justification
  ]
}

fn seed_growth_justification_well_formed(j: SeedGrowthJustification) -> Bool {
  j.reason != ""
    && j.trigger != ""
    && j.current_boundary != ""
    && length(xs: j.hand_authored_declarations) > 0
}

// DERIVED FROM THE ROSTER, NOT RE-LISTED BESIDE IT. This appended the two known
// justifications' declarations by name, which made it a SECOND enumeration of the roster one
// function above — and the two could disagree silently: adding a third row to
// seed_growth_justification_roster left its declarations invisible here, so the duplicate
// check and the G1 join would both have passed over items that were, by every other reading,
// enrolled. Folding the roster makes that state unwritable rather than caught, which is the
// construction-over-validation direction (DESIGN section 5) and is what the roster note
// already asks for when it says the roster is derived by enumeration and never by grep.
fn seed_growth_roster_all_declarations() -> List<DeclarationRef> {
  fold_list(
    xs: seed_growth_justification_roster(),
    empty: [] as List<DeclarationRef>,
    cons: fn(acc, j) { list_append(left: acc, right: j.hand_authored_declarations) }
  )
}

fn seed_growth_roster_declaration_keys() -> List<String> {
  seed_growth_roster_all_declarations()
    |> map(r => declaration_ref_display_key(ref: r))
}

fn seed_growth_roster_duplicate_keys() -> List<String> {
  let keys = seed_growth_roster_declaration_keys()
  filter(xs: keys, predicate: fn(key) { path_occurrence_count(paths: keys, target: key) > 1 })
}

fn seed_growth_roster_has_duplicate_keys() -> Bool {
  let keys = seed_growth_roster_declaration_keys()
  any(
    xs: keys,
    predicate: fn(key) { path_occurrence_count(paths: keys, target: key) > 1 }
  )
}

fn seed_growth_uncitable_item_keys() -> List<String> {
  [
    "v1_compiler.cli_run::impl std::fmt::Display for Stage0CargoBinManifestParseRefusal::fmt"
  ]
}

// TWO POPULATIONS, TWO FUNCTIONS, AND NEITHER MAY SERVE FOR THE OTHER.
//
// The single-candidate-set form that stood here answered both questions from one list, so a
// changed-item population rendered every justification for an untouched item stale, and a live
// population no longer isolated what a change added. The denominators genuinely differ: staleness
// is a question about the CURRENT surface, unjustified addition is a question about the CHANGE.
// gunbc.rust_item_host_observation produces them separately for exactly this reason.
fn seed_growth_stale_justifications(live_items: List<DeclarationRef>) -> List<String> {
  filter(
    xs: seed_growth_roster_all_declarations(),
    predicate: fn(r) { !declaration_ref_in_list(target: r, refs: live_items) }
  )
    |> map(r => declaration_ref_display_key(ref: r))
}

fn seed_growth_unjustified_additions(added: List<DeclarationRef>) -> List<String> {
  let roster = seed_growth_roster_all_declarations()
  filter(
    xs: added,
    predicate: fn(r) { !declaration_ref_in_list(target: r, refs: roster) }
  )
    |> map(r => declaration_ref_display_key(ref: r))
}

// AN ITEM WHOSE MODULE PATH COULD NOT BE DERIVED IS A REFUSAL, NOT AN OMISSION. A hand Rust item
// under a tree rust_source_namespace_rows does not claim has no DeclarationRef, so it can neither be
// found in the roster nor reported as unjustified by key -- and dropping it would let a whole
// subtree of the seed grow invisibly. It refuses, naming the item key and the missing mapping.
fn seed_growth_added_projections(added_items: List<RustItemIdentity>) -> List<ItemDeclarationRefProjection> {
  added_items |> map(item => item_declaration_ref(item: item))
}

// THE DELETED POPULATION IS NOT A PARAMETER OF THIS FUNCTION, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE MECHANISM.
// "Rust deleted elsewhere licenses Rust added here" is the offset this policy rejects, and the
// robust way to reject it is to give the verdict no access to the deletions rather than to remember
// not to consult them. seed_growth_deletions_offset_nothing is the executing evidence: it runs the
// same addition through observations whose deleted populations differ and requires one verdict.
fn seed_growth_admit_change(
  change: RustItemChangeObservation,
  live: LiveHandRustObservation,
  bridges: List<AuthorizedTemporarySeedBridge>,
  evidence: AdmissionEvidence
) -> SeedGrowthAdmissionVerdict {
  match change {
    RustItemChangeUnattributed { repo_path: path, line: line, detail: detail } =>
      SeedGrowthAdmissionRefused {
        unjustified_additions: [],
        detail: concat(
          "changed hand Rust could not be attributed to an item in ",
          concat(path, concat(": ", detail))
        )
      }
    RustItemChangeScanRefused { repo_path: path, line: _, line_text: _, detail: detail } =>
      SeedGrowthAdmissionRefused {
        unjustified_additions: [],
        detail: concat("hand Rust source could not be read at item grain in ", concat(path, concat(": ", detail)))
      }
    RustItemChangeHostRefused { detail: detail } =>
      SeedGrowthAdmissionRefused {
        unjustified_additions: [],
        detail: concat("the change population was not observed: ", detail)
      }
    RustItemChangeObserved {
      added_hand_items: added_items,
      modified_hand_items: modified_items,
      deleted_hand_items: _,
      generated_changes: _
    } => {
      let projections = seed_growth_added_projections(added_items: added_items)
      let unmappable = projected_refused_keys(projections: projections)
      let unjustified = seed_growth_unjustified_additions(
        added: projected_declaration_refs(projections: projections)
      )
      let origin_refused = origin_refusals(
        bridges: bridges,
        evidence: evidence,
        added: projected_declaration_refs(projections: projections)
      )
      if length(xs: unmappable) > 0 {
        SeedGrowthAdmissionRefused {
          unjustified_additions: unmappable,
          detail: "added hand Rust item(s) live under a tree rust_source_namespace_rows does not claim, so no DeclarationRef can address them"
        }
      } else if length(xs: unjustified) > 0 {
        SeedGrowthAdmissionRefused {
          unjustified_additions: unjustified,
          detail: "hand Rust item(s) lack SeedGrowthJustification row"
        }
      } else if length(xs: origin_refused) > 0 {
        SeedGrowthAdmissionRefused {
          unjustified_additions: origin_refused,
          detail: "added hand Rust item(s) did not establish that the capability they realize was modeled independently of them"
        }
      } else {
        match live {
          LiveHandRustHostRefused { detail: detail } =>
            SeedGrowthAdmissionRefused {
              unjustified_additions: [],
              detail: concat("the live hand-Rust population was not observed, so staleness cannot be reported: ", detail)
            }
          LiveHandRustObserved { items: live_items, unscannable: _ } =>
            SeedGrowthAdmissionComplete {
              justified_items: added_items |> map(item => rust_item_identity_key(item: item)),
              modified_items_requiring_disposition: modified_items |> map(item => rust_item_identity_key(item: item)),
              stale_justifications: seed_growth_stale_justifications(
                live_items: projected_declaration_refs(
                  projections: live_items |> map(item => item_declaration_ref(item: item))
                )
              ),
              duplicate_justifications: seed_growth_roster_duplicate_keys(),
              uncitable_items: list_append(
                left: seed_growth_uncitable_item_keys(),
                right: projected_uncitable_keys(projections: projections)
              )
            }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

fn seed_growth_roster_mechanical_checks_holds() -> Bool {
  let roster = seed_growth_justification_roster()
  length(xs: roster) >= 1
    && fold_list(
      xs: roster,
      empty: true,
      cons: fn(ok, j) { ok && seed_growth_justification_well_formed(j: j) }
    )
    && length(xs: seed_growth_roster_all_declarations()) > 0
    && !seed_growth_roster_has_duplicate_keys()
}

fn seed_growth_roster_well_formed_gate_holds() -> Bool {
  seed_growth_roster_mechanical_checks_holds()
}
